\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now the labourer's task is o'er,
\par Now the battle- day is past;
\par Now upon the farther shore
\par Lands the voyager at last.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There the tears of earth are dried;
\par There its hidden things are clear;
\par There the work of life is tried
\par By a juster Judge than here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There the Shepherd, bringing home
\par Many a lamb forlorn and strayed,
\par Shelters each, no more to roam,
\par Where the wolf can ne'er invade.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There the penitents who turn
\par To the Cross their dying eyes
\par All the love of Jesus learn
\par At His feet in paradise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. There no more the powers of hell,
\par Can prevail to mar their peace;
\par Christ the Lord shall guard them well,
\par He who died for their release.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Earth to earth, and dust to dust!
\par Calmly now the worlds we say;
\par Left behind, we wait in trust
\par For the resurresction day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Father, in Thy gracious keeping,
\par Leave we now Thy servant sleeping.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

